      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 66. महाशैल &c.—शिलानां संघातः शिलासंघातः । महांश्चासौ शैलश्च",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "महाशैलः तस्य शिलासंघातः like a dense ( सं ) line ( घात ) of rocks",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "&c. The fig. here is उपमा, वत् the simile-expressing aff.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "being omitted in the compound उत्पलकोमलम्. For a similar",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "idea, see sl. 63.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 67. नामापि न श्रूयते—even its name is not heard i. e. no",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "trace of it is left. ज्ञायते V. l. known i. e. through the medium",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "of the ears. मुक्ताकारतया—by reason of its assuming the form of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "a pearl. स्वात्याम्–In Swâti i e. while the sun is in conjunction with",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "the constellation Svâti. It is supposed that at the time of the sun",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "coming in conjunction with this constellation the pearl-shells",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "burst open and the rain-drops that they receive into their cavity",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "form pearls; see Bṛhatsanmhitâ of Varâhamihira XV. 13. Cf.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "पात्रविशेषे न्यस्तं गुणान्तरं व्रजति शिल्पमाधातुः । जलमिव समुद्रशुक्तौ मुक्ताफलतां",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "पयोदस्य ॥ Mâl. I. 6. सन्मौक्तिकम्—A good or faultless pearl. सत् is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "evidently preferable to तत्. जायते–Since this verb is repeated a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "strict rhetorician would detect in this कथितपददोष ( the fault of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "repeating a word with the same meaning ). The reading—जुषां",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "&c. is free from this fault. The fig. is अर्थान्तरन्यास.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 68. Some take एव with भर्तुः. but that is not good; the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "construction should be यद्भर्तुर्हितमेवेच्छति तत्कलत्रम्–meaning ‘she",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "that desires the good only of her husband deserves to be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "called ‘wife.’ कलत्रम् Mark the gender of this word which is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "neu.; the gender of Sanskrit words in some cases is quite",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "arbitrary as remarked by Pân.– लिङ्गमशिष्यं लोकाश्रयत्वाल्लिङ्गस्य । Cf.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "the word दार which is masc., and is always used in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "the plural. पुण्यकृतः—पुण्यं कृतवान् पुण्यकृत्. The aff. क्विप् ( ०—त् )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "is added to कृ after the words mentioned in the Sûtra सुकर्म-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "पापमन्त्रपुण्येषु कृतः । Pân. III. 2. 89.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 69. नम्रत्वेनोन्नमन्तः—rising to greatness by humility. ख्या-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "पयन्तः—pres. p. of the causal of ख्या. Their appreciation of other",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "people’s merits is in itself a sign of their possessing merits.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "वितत०—दूषयन्तः—rebuking. Contemptuous silence is the best",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
